# Orch Core Conventions

## Monorepo layout

- `apps/web` — React 19 + Vite frontend
- `apps/server` — Hono on Bun
- `packages/api` — oRPC routers and business logic
- `packages/db` — Drizzle schema and migrations
- `packages/auth` — Better Auth
- `packages/env` — Zod-validated environment
- `packages/agent`, `packages/workspace`, `packages/config` — shared libs

## Commands (Bun only — never npm/pnpm/yarn)

```bash
bun install
bun run dev              # web + server
bun run check            # oxlint + oxfmt
bun run check-types      # turbo typecheck
bun run check:conventions # golden-file layer rules (views, containers, routers, services)
bun run check:golden     # source inventory when adding/relocating files
bun run db:push          # local schema sync
```

## Definition of done

Before finishing any change:

1. `bun run check` passes
2. `bun run check-types` passes
3. `bun run check:conventions` passes for feature/API/web layer changes
4. Conventional commit message (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`)

Product features must follow the golden file pattern — see `golden-file-pattern` rule and [`docs/golden-file-pattern.md`](../../docs/golden-file-pattern.md).

## Environment access

- **Server/API/DB:** `import { env } from "@orch/env/server"`
- **Web runtime:** `import { getRpcBaseUrl } from "@/lib/env"`
- Never read raw `process.env` in app code — add vars to `packages/env` first

